;; repr/go's native-check negative controls (doc/GATE-SURVEY.md, GTS81 (a) and "As built: GTS88 (b)"): each a crossed
;; pair of two dumps of the run, both passing their own comparison with the helper (E-tree, E-ann, E-forms equal in
;; the records, test/repr/go/native-check-results.edn). The SUBJECT's native read is judged against the REFERENCE's
;; helper dump by each level's own comparison (arbace.repr.go.parse's ps/diff for :tree, annotate's same-package for
;; :ann, forms-diff for :forms: the .ae text in modes :lines and :full), which must find a difference. A level whose
;; comparison passes what differs fails the check (exit 1: a control that passes). A control whose subject or
;; reference is not in the run (a corpus not selected, --only, the gate's rotation: the ids are in repr-go-native's
;; :always) or whose subject's own comparison did not pass is left, its row says so. No control is a dump of the
;; records, the known differences or the counts. Judged after the corpora of the run, from the jobs' kept parts.
;;   :id         the name
;;   :subject    NAME/KEY of the dump whose native read is judged (NAME a corpus, KEY a dump's key)
;;   :reference  NAME/KEY of the dump whose helper dump it is judged against
;;   :levels     :tree :ann :forms (default these three); :syntax, a file go/parser rejects on both sides (the user's
;;               decision of 2026-11-22): the SUBJECT's gc errors from the native reader with one message altered
;;               (annotate's alter-message) judged by the rejected files' comparison (syntax-diff) against the REFERENCE's
;;               gc reference (gc itself over the original; its own when SUBJECT and REFERENCE are one), which must differ;
;;               and :known: native-check's known differences
;;               (test/repr/go/native-known.edn, judged by arbace.repr.go.annotate/known-difference?, check-corpus's
;;               judge): once a level above found the crossed difference, the subject's result judged against the
;;               entries the reference's own known difference would be (its dump's key, its files' keys, its package
;;               unless the subject's), which must not excuse it; judged only when listed
[{:id "control/errors-vs-io" :subject "amd64/errors" :reference "amd64/io" :levels [:tree :ann :forms :known]}
 {:id "control/list-vs-ring" :subject "amd64/container/list" :reference "amd64/container/ring" :levels [:tree :ann :forms :known]}
 {:id "control/helloworld-vs-printbig" :subject "test/helloworld.go" :reference "test/printbig.go" :levels [:tree :ann :forms :known]}
 {:id "control/closure5-a-vs-ddd2" :subject "dirtest/closure5.dir/a" :reference "dirtest/ddd2.dir/ddd2" :levels [:tree :ann :forms :known]}
 {:id "control/bombad-one-message-altered" :subject "linux-errtest/bombad.go" :reference "linux-errtest/bombad.go" :levels [:syntax]}]
